# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
#
# This repo is on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. Git's own binary heuristic
# caught the resume PDF (the stored blob is byte-identical to the original),
# but it emitted a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning while doing so, and
# relying on a heuristic for file types we already know are binary is the kind
# of thing that works until it silently does not. A corrupted PDF would not
# fail the build — it would simply refuse to open for whoever downloaded it.
#
# `-text` means: never convert, in either direction, on commit or checkout.

*.pdf   -text
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.gif   -text
*.webp  -text
*.ico   -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf   -text
*.otf   -text
*.xlsx  -text
